\DOC VPERMD_FACTOR_STRIP_TAC

\TYPE {VPERMD_FACTOR_STRIP_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes arithmetic goals stating that a weighted sum of word values modulo a
power of two equals the truncation of that sum to its low-order terms, using
the bounding assumptions in the goal.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It applies to a goal {A ?- t = u} in which {t}
is a {MOD} of a sum of scaled {val}-terms by a power of two and {u} is the
corresponding initial segment of that sum, with {A} containing numeric bounds
on each of the word values occurring; these assumptions are used but left
untouched as the goal is discharged.
{
       A ?- t = u
       ==========   VPERMD_FACTOR_STRIP_TAC
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of outcome, on goals of this
modulus-of-a-weighted-sum shape accompanied by bound assumptions on the values
involved.

\ENDDOC
